1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,680
Hello again!

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:07,040
Today, we mix big friend adding and big friend taking away — in one big game!

3
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:09,360
Let's remember everything first.

4
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:12,800
Adding: one formula for every friend.

5
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:17,180
Plus one, plus two, plus three, all the way to plus nine.

6
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:22,120
Taking away: same friends, same idea, just the other way round.

7
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,280
Minus one, all the way to minus nine.

8
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:26,800
Eighteen formulas.

9
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:28,140
You know them all.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,400
Now let's see if you remember them — mixed up, and fast!

11
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,200
It is time to Beat the Beads!

12
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:38,880
I will spin the wheel.

13
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:42,820
It will land on a number and a trick — adding, or taking away.

14
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:46,320
You tell me that number's friend, before I count to three.

15
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:49,900
If the beads get stuck, you will know exactly what to do.

16
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:52,620
Let's find out who remembers best.

17
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,900
Round one — spin the wheel!

18
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:57,340
It lands on plus four.

19
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,540
Make thirty-seven, then try to add four more.

20
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:02,900
Look at that — no room left!

21
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,060
Quick — what is four's friend?

22
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:09,260
Four's friend is six!

23
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:12,840
Plus four equals minus six, plus ten.

24
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:15,780
Thirty-seven plus four is forty-one!

25
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,680
Round two — spin the wheel!

26
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,200
It lands on minus seven.

27
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:24,300
Make eighty-one, then try to take away seven.

28
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:26,200
Uh oh, we are stuck!

29
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,800
Think fast — what is seven's friend?

30
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:33,140
Seven's friend is three!

31
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:36,780
Minus seven equals plus three, minus ten.

32
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:39,920
Eighty-one take away seven is seventy-four!

33
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:43,060
Round three — spin the wheel!

34
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,440
It lands on plus eight.

35
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:48,620
Make sixty-three, then try to add eight more.

36
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:49,760
Stuck again?

37
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:50,980
Let's fix that.

38
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:53,360
Here it comes — what is eight's friend?

39
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:57,540
Eight's friend is two!

40
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:00,980
Plus eight equals minus two, plus ten.

41
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:03,880
Sixty-three plus eight is seventy-one!

42
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,020
Round four — spin the wheel!

43
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:09,480
It lands on minus nine.

44
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:12,520
Make ninety-six, then try to take away nine.

45
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:15,360
Uh oh, that is a big one to take away!

46
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:17,420
Quick — what is nine's friend?

47
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,700
Nine's friend is one!

48
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:25,180
Minus nine equals plus one, minus ten.

49
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:28,400
Ninety-six take away nine is eighty-seven!

50
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:33,240
Four down, four to go — you are mixing it up like a pro!

51
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:36,300
If you are having fun, tap that like button.

52
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:42,180
The wheel keeps mixing adding and taking away — you never know what is coming next!

53
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:45,020
Round five — spin the wheel!

54
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,680
It lands on plus six.

55
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:50,620
Make twenty-nine, then try to add six more.

56
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:53,260
Here we go again — no room!

57
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:56,460
You remember this one — what is six's friend?

58
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:00,920
Six's friend is four!

59
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:04,480
Plus six equals minus four, plus ten.

60
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:07,120
Twenty-nine plus six is thirty-five!

61
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,180
Round six — spin the wheel!

62
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:12,800
It lands on minus three.

63
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:15,860
Make sixty-two, then try to take away three.

64
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:16,900
Stuck!

65
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:18,480
Good thing we have a trick.

66
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:19,840
What is three's friend?

67
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:20,820
Tell me!

68
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:25,080
Three's friend is seven!

69
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:28,680
Minus three equals plus seven, minus ten.

70
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:31,620
Sixty-two take away three is fifty-nine!

71
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,640
Round seven — spin the wheel!

72
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:37,380
It lands on minus two.

73
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:40,740
Make ninety-one, then try to take away two.

74
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:43,500
Only one bead there — not enough!

75
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,100
Can you get this one?

76
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:46,580
What is two's friend?

77
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,980
Two's friend is eight!

78
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:54,640
Minus two equals plus eight, minus ten.

79
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,720
Ninety-one take away two is eighty-nine!

80
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:01,320
Round eight — spin the wheel!

81
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,060
It lands on plus five.

82
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:06,940
Make sixty-eight, then try to add five more.

83
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,180
One more stuck moment to solve!

84
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:11,700
Last one — what is five's friend?

85
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:15,980
Five's friend is five!

86
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:19,440
Plus five equals minus five, plus ten.

87
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:22,200
Sixty-eight plus five is seventy-three!

88
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:25,580
You just beat all eight big friend formulas!

89
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:30,380
Adding and taking away, all mixed up, and you got every one.

90
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:33,640
Nine formulas each way, and now you have played with both.

91
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:37,080
Try Beat the Beads on your own abacus at home.

92
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:42,200
For more sums to practice, search for Abacus Kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

93
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,300
Download it free.

94
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:49,680
Next time, we will meet a brand new kind of trick — one that adds and takes away, both at once.

95
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:50,920
See you next time!
